# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
# Adjustfile — advisory accessibility, clarity, and drift tolerances for Hermeneia
# Author: Jonathan D.A. Jewell <j.d.a.jewell@open.ac.uk>
#
# Paired runner: adjust.ncl
# The runner schema treats these as advisory requirements/tolerances. No
# automatic file edits are authorized by this draft.

@abstract:
Adjust is Hermeneia's non-blocking review surface for accessibility, inclusive
design, diagnostic clarity, and honest feature-status reporting. Hermeneia is a
plain-text CLI and documentation project; it has no browser UI, so this file
does not claim WCAG conformance or invent a numeric accessibility score.

Corrective actions are recommendations for a maintainer. Automated fixes stay
disabled unless a later owner-approved rule supplies a deterministic, reversible
fix and an independently verified probe.
@end

## CLI Accessibility and Clarity

### explicit-text-status
- description: Results and diagnostics identify the subject, use-model, verdict, and failure reason in text rather than color or icon alone
- tolerance: Every essential status has a plain-text label; diagnostics distinguish parse/plan faults from checker faults
- corrective: Preserve explicit labels and actionable error messages; add a regression test whenever output semantics change
- probe: cargo test --workspace
- severity: advisory
- notes: The CLI currently prints plain text; no color-only contract or WCAG claim is intended.

### unsupported-operation-disclosure
- description: Recognized but unimplemented voke operations are reported as not implemented, not as syntax errors or successful empty results
- tolerance: All six not-yet-implemented operations remain explicit and non-successful
- corrective: Keep parser/store/CLI diagnostics and the implemented-versus-planned table in sync
- probe: cargo test -p hermeneia-syntax other_vokes_are_unimplemented_not_syntax_errors
- severity: advisory

### accessible-documentation-format
- description: General documentation stays in the repository's accessible, text-based AsciiDoc format
- tolerance: No Markdown files are added under docs/; essential instructions remain usable without rendered graphics
- corrective: Write new general documentation in AsciiDoc and provide textual descriptions for diagrams
- probe: bash scripts/check-no-md-in-docs.sh
- severity: advisory

## Scope and Evidence Drift

### implementation-status-honesty
- description: Public feature claims distinguish design, parsing, implementation, testing, and integration
- tolerance: The current slice is described as one implemented operation (`invoke`) over the local JSONL store; Vocarium integration and the other six operations remain pending
- corrective: Update README.adoc, docs/SPEC.adoc, EXPLAINME.adoc, and STATE.a2ml together with the code and tests
- probe: cargo test --workspace
- severity: advisory
- notes: This is an advisory review target; unit tests do not prove every prose claim.

### accessibility-standard-not-overclaimed
- description: Accessibility conformance is not claimed for a product surface that has no graphical interface
- tolerance: No WCAG score or web-interface compliance claim unless a user-facing graphical surface is added and evaluated
- corrective: If a GUI is introduced, obtain owner approval for the applicable standard and measurable acceptance criteria before claiming compliance
- severity: advisory
